            "displayName": "Mark Waite",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Denver"
          },
          "body": "The security issue is described in the [July 27, 2022 security advisory|https://www.jenkins.io/security/advisory/2022-07-27/#SECURITY-2404].  I'm reasonably confident that no work is currently being done to resolve the issue.\n\nThe security team contacts plugin maintainers and gives them a reasonable time to fix the issue before they publish a security advisory.  If the maintainer does not respond or does not provide the fix, then the advisory is published to note that there is a known issue in the plugin.\n\nWe'd love to have you or someone at your employer [adopt the plugin|https://www.jenkins.io/doc/developer/plugin-governance/adopt-a-plugin/], resolve the security issue, and release a new version of the plugin.  There is a [five part video series|https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Fev8KfFsPZE] on adopting a plugin and a [three part video series|https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=D-b9WWx1Xes] on resolving a vulnerability in a plugin.  If you prefer written instructions, there is the [\"Contributing to Open Source\" document|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PKYIpPlRVGsBqrz0Ob1Cv3cefOZ5j2xtGZdWs27kLuw/edit?usp=sharing] that guides many of the same steps.",
